(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108: the destination side of the 573/574 shape -
 `u` already holds an OWNED string (from its own format-string
 declaration) when `Set u to src as text.` overwrites it with an aliased,
 non-owned pointer. The fix must still free `u`'s own prior string here
 (nothing else names it) while correctly refusing to free `src`'s string
 that `u` now shares - both halves of the free-on-`Set` decision in one
 statement.)

a number called n is 2.
a text called src is "v{n}".
a text called u is "{n}!".
Set u to src as text.
Set src to "z{n}".
Print "u={u} src={src}".
